<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hungarian Democratic Forum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1987">1987</a>–<a href="/years/2011">2011</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as MDF</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hungarian Democratic Forum was a centre-right political party founded in 1987 at Lakitelek by intellectuals opposed to communist rule. It won <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>'s first free elections in 1990, and its leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jozsef-antall">József Antall</a> became prime minister. After losing power in 1994 it declined steadily and dissolved itself in 2011.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Free elections in May 1990 brought the conservative <b>Hungarian Democratic Forum</b> to the head of a coalition, and József Antall became the first democratically elected prime minister since the war.</blockquote><a href="/empire/hungary">Hungary · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
